  "finding": "Near the fit boundary the WDDM allocator takes one of two branches - pack dedicated VRAM to the ceiling, or satisfy part of the allocation from shared - and which branch it takes is decided by what is already resident, not by chance. Two runs of q3kxl/262144/n18 nineteen seconds apart, one cold (14.6 s) and one warm (6.5 s), returned byte-identical dedicated, shared and idle figures. The branch is therefore reproducible for a given desktop state and varies only when the desktop varies. This is what makes 'clean at n, spilling at n+2, clean at n+4' possible without any non-monotonic memory demand: the three cells are not three points on one curve, they are two different branches.",
